{
	"type": "equipment",
	"name": "Aiuen, The Elf-Gate Key Rune",
	"folder": "d0L7Q0JIPgaqFobo",
	"img": "icons/sundries/misc/key-short-red.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": {
			"gm": "",
			"value": "<p><strong>Usage</strong> drawn on a creature</p><hr><p>This masterful circular rune is key to the <em>aiudara</em> network of elf gates that stretch across the stars. Once per turn, when the rune-bearer takes a Stride action, they can instead teleport a distance equal to their Speed.</p><p><strong>Invocation</strong> You teleport the rune-bearer to a location adjacent to any of your other runes, as long as it is on the same plane. An unwilling target can be teleported a maximum distance of 60 feet, and it avoids being teleported at all if it succeeds at a @Check[will|against:class] save against your class DC.</p><hr><p><strong>Special</strong> If you have the ability to cast the sigil cantrip, then you can use aiuen, the elf-gate key's invocation to teleport the rune-bearer to a location adjacent to any of your sigils on the same plane, in addition to any of your runes.</p>"
		},
